   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Brookhaven to\naccept an application for a real property tax exemption from St. Mary AME Zion\nChurch",
    "basePrintNo": "S7724",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7724-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Suffolk County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7724\n\nSPONSOR: MURRAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the assessor of the town of Brookhaven\nto accept an application for a real property tax exemption from St. Mary\nAME Zion Church\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Town of Brookhaven assessor to accept an appli-\ncation for exemption from real property taxes with respect to the 2022-\n23, 20232024, and 2024-25 assessment rolls from St. Mary AME Zion Church\nfor property located at 537 Granny Road in the hamlet of Medford.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nExisting law authorizes tax exemptions to be granted after the taxable\nstatus date has passed if a bill is chaptered authorizing the assessor\nto accept the late application. The Town of Brookhaven Assessor's Office\nhas stated that the exemption would have been granted if the application\nhad been timely.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
